# Skedaddle Portal

Private ops portal for a northern Colorado tire resale business. Live at skedaddleinc.com. Repo: abinghambyte/skedaddleinc.

Before making **recommendations** or architectural suggestions, read `docs/AI-CONTEXT.md` and `docs/ROADMAP.md`.

## Stack

- React 19 + Vite + Tailwind → Vercel (git push deploys frontend)
- Firebase Cloud Functions Gen2 Node 22 → `npm run deploy:firebase`
- Firestore (project: skedaddle-inventory)
- **firebase-functions v7.2.5 — do not downgrade**

## Deploy

- Functions: `npm run deploy:firebase`
- Frontend: `git add . && git commit -m "message" && git push`
- Always run `npm run lint && npm run build` before declaring work done
- When both change: **deploy functions before pushing frontend**

## Secrets (Slack / Functions)

- Slack secrets live in **Firebase Secret Manager** — never in `functions/.env`
- Functions that use Slack must import from `functions/slackSecrets.js`
- Always use **`SLACK_BOT_TOKEN.value()`** (and the pattern from that module) — never `process.env` for Slack credentials
- New secrets: `firebase functions:secrets:set SECRET_NAME`

## Pricing model

- **`price`** = Kyle's buy price per tire (in Firestore for catalog tires)
- **`paymentAmount`** = total the customer paid (revenue). **No `salePrice` field**
- **profit** = `(paymentAmount - buyPrice - mountCost - deliveryCost - otherCost) × qty`
- **FET washes out** — never subtract FET in margin or profit calcs
- **`kylePriceOverride`** = use as buy price when set on an order; else catalog price
- **CTS** = mount + delivery + other only; FET is never part of CTS
- Tires can sell before inventory arrives — **qty may be zero or negative**; never gate core logic on `qty > 0`

## Order lifecycle

Six stages only: `pending` → `available` → `scheduled` → `in_transit` → `completed`. Never use the old 3-stage model (pending/ready/sold).

## Formatting

- Currency: `formatCurrency` from `src/utils/format.js` (frontend) or `functions/format.js` (backend)
- Percentages: `formatPercent` from the same files
- Quantities: `formatQty` from the same files
- CSV exports: plain numeric strings — no currency symbols

## UI

- **Desktop layout must not change** when adding mobile fixes; use **`max-sm:`** and **`sm:`** only for mobile
- Crew tags in UI: **Overwatch, Source, Field, Spotter** — use `src/utils/portalCrewTag.js`; never raw role strings in UI
- Margin % colors (from `src/utils/marginCalc.js:marginBadgeClass`): **red below 15%**, **amber 15–24%**, **green 25–34%**, **sky 35%+**
- Modals: always **Escape** and **backdrop click** to dismiss

## Naming — do not change

- **"Rubber CRM"** — do not rename (e.g. not "Fleet CRM")
- **`paymentAmount`** — never rename to salePrice or anything else
- **`SLACK_SECRETS` / `functions/slackSecrets.js`** — never inline Slack secrets

## Utilities — prefer these, avoid duplicating

- `src/utils/format.js` — currency, percent, qty
- `src/utils/parseTireDescription.js` — tire description parser
- `src/utils/portalCrewTag.js` — portal crew tag labels
- `src/utils/orderPoolMargin.js` — pool and margin
- `src/utils/isoWeekDenver.js` — Denver ISO week
- `functions/slackSecrets.js` — secret definitions
- `functions/format.js` — server formatters
- `functions/financeStats.js` — e.g. `runCompletionTransaction`

## Crew profit split (reference)

- Alex (Overwatch / admin): 50% of profit pool
- DJ (Field / mechanic): 20%
- Tanner (Field / mechanic): 20%
- Kyle (Source / supplier): 10%
